I.. ANNOUNCEMENT IN OPEN SESSION OF ITEMS TO BE DISCUSSED IN CLOSED SESSION

CONFERENCE WITH LEGAL COUNSEL (EXISTING LITIGATION) 
(Government Code Section 54956.9(d)(1))

         1) Name of Case: Armando Marquez v. City of Manhattan Beach
                                       County of Los Angeles Superior Court

             Case No: 25STCV34923


          2) Name of Case: Highrose El Porto LLC. v City of Manhattan Beach, et al. 
                                        County of Los Angeles Superior Court 

              Case No: 25STCP04250

         3)  Name of Case: Manhattan Beach Firefighters' Association, Local 3925,                                     
                                        a Labor Association, et al. v City of Manhattan Beach                                     
                                        United States District Court District of California      
                                          
              Case No: 24-4228

II.. RECESS INTO CLOSED SESSION {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\i\fs22 At 5:01 PM, the City Council recessed into Closed Session.\i0\fs24\par
\cf1\fs22\par
}


III.. RECONVENE INTO OPEN SESSION {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\i\fs22 At 6:00 PM, the City Council reconvened into Open Session with all City Councilmembers present. \i0\fs24\par
\cf1\fs22\par
}


IV.. CLOSED SESSION ANNOUNCEMENT IN OPEN SESSION {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\i\fs22 City Attorney Quinn Barrow announced that the City Council went into Closed Session to discuss three items of litigation. With respect to Items 2 and 3 as listed on the agenda, the City Council gave direction on a 5 to 0 vote. With respect to Item 1 on the agenda, the City Council gave direction on a 3 to 2 vote, with Councilmember Charelian and Mayor Pro Tem Franklin voting no.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\cf1\fs22\par
}


G.. ADJOURNMENT {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\i\fs22 At 6:01 PM, Mayor Lesser adjourned the meeting.\i0\fs24\par
\cf1\fs22\par
}


